## Report: OfficeFloor Spring PetClinic REST — Owner creation & telephone handling

### 1. Create-owner YAML pipeline (POST /owners)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`**
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

The pipeline is a 3-step chain: `build` → `save` → `respond`. (Related but separate endpoint: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners/{ownerId}/pets.POST.yml` for pets, not owner creation. The owner list is `owners.GET.yml`.)

### 2. Function classes in the create-owner pipeline

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`**
```java
@Validated
public class BuildOwner {
    public void service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
        built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
    }
}
```
This is where the incoming body is bean-validated (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) and mapped to an `Owner` entity. It is the single point where telephone validation on create is triggered.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/SaveOwner.java`**
```java
public class SaveOwner {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);
    }
}
```

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`**
```java
public class RespondWithOwnerCreated {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

Two related owner functions (used by the PUT/update pipeline, NOT the create chain, but relevant for how telephone is applied):

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ApplyOwner.java`** — copies fields including `owner.setTelephone(request.getTelephone())`.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwner.java`** — `@Validated` class validating `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` before `LoadOwner` (so invalid body → 400 even when owner missing).

Note: the create pipeline does **no** telephone normalization — `BuildOwner` maps straight through via MapStruct and `SaveOwner` persists as-is.

### 3. Entity and DTOs — telephone field & validation

**Owner entity `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** (extends `Person`):
```java
@Column(name = "telephone")
@NotEmpty
@Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
private String telephone;
```
Also `@NotEmpty` on `address` and `city`. `Person` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`) adds `@NotEmpty firstName`/`lastName`.

**DTOs are NOT hand-written source files.** They are generated by the OpenAPI Generator Maven plugin from the spec and land in `target/generated-sources/openapi/...` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`). The authoritative definition is in the spec:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** — `OwnerFields` schema (→ `OwnerFieldsDto`, the create request body) and `Owner` schema (→ `OwnerDto`, response = OwnerFields + `id`):
```yaml
OwnerFields:
  properties:
    firstName: { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 30, pattern: "^[\p{L}]+([ '-][\p{L}]+){0,2}$" }
    lastName:  { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 30, pattern: "^[\p{L}]+([ '-][\p{L}]+){0,2}\.?$" }
    address:   { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 255, pattern: '.*\S.*' }
    city:      { type: string, minLength: 1, maxLength: 80, pattern: '.*\S.*' }
    telephone:
      title: Telephone number
      type: string
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 20
      pattern: '^[0-9]*$'
      example: '6085551023'
  required: [ firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone ]
Owner:
  allOf:
    - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OwnerFields'
    - type: object
      properties:
        id: { type: integer, format: int32, minimum: 0 }
```

Key discrepancy to note: the **DTO telephone** validation (from openapi.yml) is `pattern '^[0-9]*$'`, `minLength 1`, `maxLength 20` — i.e. up to 20 digits, allows empty-ish. The **entity telephone** is stricter: exactly 10 digits (`^[0-9]{10}$`). On create, `BuildOwner` validates the DTO (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`), so the 20-digit DTO rule governs the 400, not the entity's 10-digit rule.

**Mapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — MapStruct `@Mapper`; `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id` and `pets`, no telephone transformation.

### 4. Escalation YAML and handlers (validation / 400 / errors)

Escalation YAMLs in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`:
- `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` → handler `ValidationExceptionHandler` (this is the **400 validation** path)
- `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` → `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler`
- `java.lang.Exception.yml` → `GeneralExceptionHandler`
- `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.NotFoundException.yml` → `NotFoundExceptionHandler`
- `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` → (ForbiddenExceptionHandler, present in source dir)

Each YAML is just `handle:\n  class: <FQCN>`.

Handler classes in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`:
- **`ValidationExceptionHandler.java`** — handles `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, builds a `ProblemDetail` (status 400, detail "The request contains invalid or missing parameters"), and attaches `schemaValidationErrors` (list of `ValidationMessageDto` with per-field message, `field`, `rejectedValue`, `defaultMessage`) plus a distinct `errors` field list. This is what a bad telephone on create produces.
- **`ProblemDetails.java`** — package-private helper building the common `ProblemDetail` (title = exception simple name, `timestamp`, empty `schemaValidationErrors` placeholder).
- `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler.java` — returns 404 (note: maps data constraint violation to NOT_FOUND).
- `GeneralExceptionHandler.java` — logs and returns 500.
- `NotFoundExceptionHandler.java` — returns 404 empty.
- Also present: `ForbiddenExceptionHandler.java`, `NotFoundException.java`. Validation helpers under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/` (`PetAgeValidator.java`, `PetAgeValidation.java`) — pet-specific, not owner/telephone.

### 5. Tests related to creating owners / telephone (under `src/test`)

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:

**`AcceptanceTest.java`** — directly telephone-focused:
```java
/** telephone-normalize: On create, normalize the telephone by removing every non-digit character, then require exa... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
    @Test void coreStripsToTenDigits() {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("telephone", "(04) 1234-5678");
        int id = createOwnerOk(o);
        getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("0412345678"));
    }
    @Test void errorRejectsTooFewDigits() {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("telephone", "12345");
        createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
    }
}
```
These assert a telephone-normalization rule (strip non-digits → require exactly 10 digits) that the current create pipeline does **not** implement — the pipeline has no normalization step and the DTO pattern `^[0-9]*$` would reject `"(04) 1234-5678"` with a 400 rather than normalizing it. So `coreStripsToTenDigits` would currently fail.

**`AcceptanceBase.java`** — black-box base (`@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser` roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN). Centers on `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`. Key helpers: `ownerNode()` (fully valid unique owner), `uniqueTelephone()` → `"04%08d"` (10-digit AU mobile), `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk`, `createOwnerWithKey` (Idempotency-Key), `getOwner`, `fetchOwner`, `extractId`, plus pinned reference data (CITY_REGION, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS) and helpers (sha256hex, luhn, toBusinessDay). Comments reference many planned rules (postcode, region, timezone, idempotency, per-city/per-day caps, E.164 +61) not yet in the code.

**`AuditLogCapture.java`** — test utility capturing the `AUDIT` Logback logger for asserting audit side-effects.

Test resources: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/resources/application.properties`.

### 6. Build file & OfficeFloor starter

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`** (Maven; the only build file — no Gradle). Relevant:
- `<officefloor.version>4.0.2</officefloor.version>`
- OfficeFloor staging repo: `https://github.com/officefloor/maven/raw/repository/`
- **OfficeFloor REST Spring Boot starter IS present:**
  ```xml
  <groupId>net.officefloor.springboot</groupId>
  <artifactId>officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter</artifactId>
  <version>${officefloor.version}</version>
  ```
- Also `net.officefloor.web` dependency (~line 159).
- `springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui` (3.0.3) and the **`openapi-generator-maven-plugin`** (7.23.0), which generates the DTOs from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` (added as a source root ~line 424). This confirms `OwnerDto`/`OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerPageDto`/`ValidationMessageDto`/`ProblemDetail`-related DTOs are generated, not in `src`.

### Summary of how it fits together
POST /api/owners is authorized for `OWNER_ADMIN`, then `BuildOwner` validates the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Valid`) and MapStructs it to an `Owner`; `SaveOwner` persists; `RespondWithOwnerCreated` returns 201 with `OwnerDto` and a Location header. Telephone validation on create comes entirely from the DTO bean-validation rules generated from `openapi.yml` (`^[0-9]*$`, max 20) — surfaced as a 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → `ValidationExceptionHandler`. There is no normalization step, and the entity's stricter 10-digit rule only applies at persistence. The acceptance tests expect normalization-to-10-digits behavior that is not yet implemented.

